          "response_id": 1
        },
        "role": "agent"
      },
      {
        "content": "Okay, sounds good.",
        "created_timestamp": 1792355168667,
        "message_id": "message_379bf09d53b0c762d164d3ca",
        "role": "user"
      },
      {
        "content": "Perfect. The short version is this: first, the buyback means the manufacturer takes the truck back and refunds what you paid toward it. Second, the manufacturer pays our fees and costs, so you never get a bill from us. Third, only money above the buyback gets split fifty-fifty. For the sake of argument, if the buyback were fifty thousand and the case settled for a hundred thousand, the first fifty is all yours, and the extra fifty gets split, so you'd walk away with seventy-five thousand. Last piece, there can be a mileage offset, which is a fixed deduction based on the miles driven before the problem first showed up. That's the whole thing in a nutshell. What questions can I answer before I walk you through signing?",
        "created_timestamp": 1792355170117,
        "message_id": "message_c819baf6a601befb34ced54b",
        "metadata": {
          "response_id": 2
        },
        "role": "agent"
      },
